306 - Draw Me Nearer
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 306
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[G]I am Thine, [D7]O Lord, I have heard [G]thy voice,
And it [C]told Thy love to [G]me;
But I long [D7]to rise in the arms [G]of faith
And be [C]clos[Am]er [D]drawn [D7]to [G]Thee.
[G]Draw me nearer, [C]nearer, blessed [G]Lord,
To the [C]cross [G]where [D7]Thou [G]hast [D]died.
[G]Draw me nearer, nearer, [C]nearer, blessed Lord,
To Thy [G]precious, [D]bleeding [G]side.

Refrain:
[G]Draw me [D7]nearer, nearer, [G]blessed Lord,
[C]to the cross [G]where thou hast died.
[D7]Draw me nearer, [G]nearer, nearer, blessed Lord,
[C]to [Am]thy [D]precious, [D7]bleeding [G]side.

Verse 2:
[G]Consecrate me [D7]now to [G]thy service, Lord,
[C]by the power [G]of grace divine;
[D7]let my soul look [G]up with a steadfast hope,
[C]and [Am]my [D]will be [D7]lost [G]in thine.

Verse 3:
[G]O the [D7]pure delight of [G]a single hour
[C]that before thy [G]throne I spend,
[D7]when I kneel in prayer, [G]and with thee, my God,
[C]I [Am]commune [D]as [D7]friend [G]with friend!
